  "description": "XIQSOF crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C18 H66 N6 Nd4 O26 8+,4(Na1 1+),12(Cl1 O4 1-),23(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2C (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.933-3.984 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.73-109.44°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd4(μ3-OH)4(Ala)6(H2O)10]8+. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 8+.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
